Use Windows.pkg
Use cFTModalPanel.pkg
Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg
Use cFTGridHost.pkg              // FT: the dialog's one host - a grid of 8 px columns, the page over a row of buttons (RDCFlexTron)
Use FTAllWebControlClasses.pkg   // FT: cFTWebButton - Copy, Reset and Close
Use cFTHtmlPage.pkg              // FT: the history's page - its title (psLabel) and the glyph beside it
Use FTMarkupBuilders.pkg         // the HTML vocabulary - OpenHtml, IconLabel, the builders
Use ModProgressCounts.pkg        // what a progress entry's counts mean, and what to call them
Use RefactorFileIO.pkg           // rfOpenOutput / rfCloseOutput - channel file I/O

// Modernization Progress History (phase 2 of the burn-down counters). Opened from the dashboard's
// progress strip (DashboardFT ProgressTileHtml -> CI_DashViewProgress -> ShowProgressHistory). Shows the
// per-workspace history (cRefactorApplication ReadModProgress -> Data\ModProgress-<wskey>.json) as a table
// (newest first) + a one-line trend, with a Reset that clears the file for a fresh baseline. The body is
// rendered from HistoryHtml, which links CssStyle/modprogress.css (it carried its own inline <style> until
// the CSS sweep of 2026-08-21) and matches the web dashboard.
//
// A PAGE OVER A ROW OF BUTTONS (2026-09-30), built the way the library's message box is: one grid host,
// which cFTModalPanel fits to the panel (phoClientHost); the history in a cFTHtmlPage - the heading is the
// page's own title, and the body under it scrolls as a whole; and Copy, Reset and Close as framework
// buttons (cFTWebButton) at the bottom right. Until then the three were chips in the page's HTML footer,
// and a click on one only ARMED a 1 ms defer timer: a web OnClick runs inside the WebView2 pump, where
// Reset's Yes/No box or ending the modal faults err 4410. A button's OnButtonClick runs after the click
// has returned, so the timer is gone.
//
// THE HISTORY ON EACH OPEN: it may have changed while the dialog was closed, so the panel's Activating
// renders it again (RefreshHistory) - stored for a page that loads (Set psHtml) and pushed to a page that
// is up (UpdateHtml, WebSet), the two ways an FT dialog's content reaches its page. That replaced the
// Set psHtml plus a timed UpdateHtml that ShowProgressHistory did.

Object oModProgressHistory_dg is a cFTModalPanel
    Set Label to "Modernization Progress History"
    Set Size to 220 470
    Set Location to 2 40
    Set piMinSize to 120 360
    Set Icon to "Modernize.ico"

    Object oWebHost is a cFTGridHost
        Set Location to 4 4
        Set Size to 196 462
        Set peAnchors to anNone         // placed by cFTModalPanel (phoClientHost)
        // Row 0, the page, takes the extra height, and row 1 is 8 px of air above the buttons in row 2. Column 0
        // takes the extra width, so the buttons keep to the right edge; the page spans every column.
        Set piColumnCount to 34         // column 0, then Copy's, Reset's and Close's 11
        Set psColumnWidths to "0/1fr"   // column 0 takes the extra width
        Set psRowHeights to "0/1fr 1/8px"

        /* The series NAME as the user should read it. The value in sProgram is a stored key - for a
           source-analyze lap it is the reserved CS_ModProgressDeepScanLabel, which is frozen at
           "Deep Scan" because it is what is already written in every workspace's ModProgress json
           (the trend matches rows BY it). Everything on screen goes through here instead, so the
           feature can be called whatever it is called today without orphaning that history.
           For a real program the key IS the .src name, which is its own display text. */
        Function SeriesText String sProgram Returns String
            If (sProgram = CS_ModProgressDeepScanLabel) ;
                Function_Return CS_ModProgressScanSeriesText
            Function_Return sProgram
        End_Function

        // Builds the page's body from the history RefreshHistory has read: the stylesheet + a one-line trend
        // summary + the burn-down sparkline + the table (one row per recorded analyze, NEWEST FIRST). The
        // heading is the page's own title, and the buttons are framework buttons under the page. Empty
        // history -> a muted placeholder.
        Function HistoryHtml tModProgressFile Hist Returns String
            String sHtml sRows sHead sSeries sNoun sCleanTd sBars sBarCls sTip
            tModProgressEntry E
            Integer iN i iFirstWarn iLastWarn
            Integer iMax iH iShown iFrom iLast
            Integer[] aiIdx
            Boolean bAnyErr bAnyClear

            Move (SizeOfArray(Hist.aEntries)) to iN

            // The stylesheet is AppHtml/CssStyle/modprogress.css, every rule in it scoped to the body's .mph;
            // the palette's tokens it uses come with the host (cFTThemeHost_mixin).
            Move (CS_ModProgressCssLink + (DivOpen("mph"))) to sHtml
            If (iN = 0) Begin
                Move (sHtml + ((DivOpen("mph-sub")) + 'Per-workspace burn-down across Compile ') + CS_RArrow + ' Analyze ' + CS_RArrow + ' Run cycles and Analyze Source ' + CS_RArrow + (' Run cycles.' + CS_DivEnd)) to sHtml
                Move (sHtml + (((DivOpen("mph-empty")) + ('No cycles recorded yet.' + CS_Br + 'Run an Analyze or an Analyze Source to start tracking the burn-down.')) + CS_DivEnd)) to sHtml
                Function_Return (sHtml + CS_DivEnd)
            End

            // trend summary: the LATEST entry vs the FIRST entry of the SAME series (matched by sProgram -
            // the file interleaves programs and, since 2026-07-16, Deep Scan laps under the reserved
            // CS_ModProgressDeepScanLabel series). Comparing across series was always shaky and turns
            // meaningless with scans in the file: a scan's finding count and a compiler's warning count
            // are different magnitudes. The scan series says "findings"; the walk below always
            // terminates because the latest entry itself matches its own series.
            Move Hist.aEntries[iN - 1] to E
            // The TOTAL is the magnitude a lap was burning down - and it is exactly the number the
            // single iWarn field held before the split, for an old row and a new one alike, so this
            // trend and the sparkline below read the same as they always did (2026-09-15).
            Move (ModProgressTotalCount(E)) to iLastWarn
            Move E.sProgram to sSeries
            Move 0 to i
            While (Hist.aEntries[i].sProgram <> sSeries)
                Increment i
            Loop
            Move (ModProgressTotalCount(Hist.aEntries[i])) to iFirstWarn
            Move (ModProgressCountNoun(sSeries)) to sNoun
            Move (sHtml + (DivOpen("mph-sub")) + String(iN) + ' entries ' + CS_MidDot + ' ' + (SeriesText(Self, sSeries)) + ' ' + sNoun + ' ' + String(iFirstWarn) + ' ' + CS_RArrow + ' ' + String(iLastWarn)) to sHtml
            If (iFirstWarn > iLastWarn) ;
                Move (sHtml + (' ' + (SpanOpen("mph-down")) + ('(' + CS_DownTriangle + ' ')) + String(iFirstWarn - iLastWarn) + (' fewer)' + CS_SpanEnd)) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml

            /* BURN-DOWN SPARKLINE - the same series the trend line above reports on, and for the same
               reason: the file interleaves programs (and Deep Scan laps under CS_ModProgressDeepScanLabel),
               so bars spanning a program switch would put a compiler's warning count and a scan's finding
               count on one scale. Height = warnings against the series maximum; COLOUR carries the one fact
               the table makes you hunt for - whether that lap still had errors. Needs two laps to be a
               trend, so a single-entry series renders nothing.

               Pure CSS: one flex row of divs with a percentage height. No canvas, no library - it has to
               survive being a string injected into the framework's DOM like the rest of this dialog. */
            Move 0 to i
            While (i < iN)
                If (Hist.aEntries[i].sProgram = sSeries) ;
                    Move i to aiIdx[-1]
                Increment i
            Loop
            Move (SizeOfArray(aiIdx)) to iShown
            If (iShown > 1) Begin
                // Cap at the most recent 24: below ~3px a bar stops being readable, and the table
                // underneath still carries every row.
                Move 0 to iFrom
                If (iShown > 24) ;
                    Move (iShown - 24) to iFrom
                Move 1 to iMax
                Move iFrom to i
                While (i < iShown)
                    If ((ModProgressTotalCount(Hist.aEntries[aiIdx[i]])) > iMax) ;
                        Move (ModProgressTotalCount(Hist.aEntries[aiIdx[i]])) to iMax
                    Increment i
                Loop
                Move (DivOpen("mph-spark")) to sBars
                Move iFrom to i
                While (i < iShown)
                    Move Hist.aEntries[aiIdx[i]] to E
                    Move (((ModProgressTotalCount(E)) * 100) / iMax) to iH
                    If (iH < 2) ;
                        Move 2 to iH
                    Move "sp-b" to sBarCls
                    If (E.iErr > 0) ;
                        Move "sp-b e" to sBarCls
                    If (i = (iShown - 1)) ;
                        Move "sp-b now" to sBarCls
                    /* Which swatches the legend needs. The LATEST bar always paints pale -
                       its own error state is not visible on it - so only the bars before it
                       can put "errors present" or "errors cleared" on screen. Naming a colour
                       nothing is drawn in sends the reader hunting for a bar that is not there. */
                    If (i < (iShown - 1)) Begin
                        If (E.iErr > 0) ;
                            Move True to bAnyErr
                        Else ;
                            Move True to bAnyClear
                    End
                    Move (E.sDate + ' - ' + String(ModProgressTotalCount(E)) + ' ' + sNoun + ', ' + String(E.iErr) + ' errors') to sTip
                    Move (sBars + '<div class="' + sBarCls + '" style="height:' + String(iH) + '%" title="' + sTip + ('">' + CS_DivEnd)) to sBars
                    Increment i
                Loop
                Move (sBars + CS_DivEnd) to sBars
                Move Hist.aEntries[aiIdx[iFrom]]      to E
                Move (sBars + ((DivOpen("mph-meta")) + CS_SpanOpen) + E.sDate + ' ' + CS_MidDot + ' ' + String(ModProgressTotalCount(E)) + CS_SpanEnd) to sBars
                Move (sBars + CS_SpanOpen) to sBars
                If (bAnyErr) ;
                    Move (sBars + '<i class="lg-e"></i>errors present') to sBars
                If (bAnyClear) ;
                    Move (sBars + '<i class="lg-c"></i>errors cleared') to sBars
                Move (sBars + ('<i class="lg-n"></i>latest' + CS_SpanEnd)) to sBars
                Move Hist.aEntries[aiIdx[iShown - 1]] to E
                Move (sBars + CS_SpanOpen + E.sDate + ' ' + CS_MidDot + ' ' + String(ModProgressTotalCount(E)) + (CS_SpanEnd + CS_DivEnd)) to sBars
                Move (sHtml + sBars) to sHtml
            End

            // table, NEWEST first. The trailing Clean column is DERIVED per row (Nils 2026-07-16), never
            // stored: a lap is terminal when it recorded no errors and nothing actionable (auto+review = 0)
            // - remaining warnings/findings are informational or out of scope by definition. One formula
            // covers both series (a compile row's iErr matters; a scan row's iErr is always 0); only the
            // tooltip wording differs ("clean" vs the scan loop's "exhausted"). Being derived, it also
            // back-fills every row recorded before the column existed.
            Move ((RowHtml("", (HeadCellHtml("l", "When")) + (HeadCellHtml("l", "Program")) ;
                + (HeadCellHtml("", "Err")) ;
                + (HeadCellTipHtml("", ("Compiler warnings on this lap. An Analyze Source lap reads source" ;
                    + " and never invokes the compiler, so its rows are 0 here - and a lap recorded before" ;
                    + " the two were counted apart keeps whatever it had under this column."), "Warn")) ;
                + (HeadCellTipHtml("", ("Source-scan findings on this lap - obsolete code the SCANNER found" ;
                    + " and the compiler never reports. An Analyze Source lap is all findings; a Compile lap" ;
                    + " shows a number here only where pending findings were merged into that analysis."), "Find")) ;
                + (HeadCellHtml("", "Auto")) + (HeadCellHtml("", "Review")) ;
                + (HeadCellHtml("l", "Target")) ;
                + (HeadCellTipHtml("l", ("The platform the measured build targeted. Blank for an Analyze Source cycle," ;
                    + " which reads source and is the same whatever the build targets - and for cycles recorded" ;
                    + " before this was tracked."), "Platform")) ;
                + (HeadCellTipHtml("", ("A check mark = this cycle came back with no errors and nothing actionable" ;
                    + " - the cycle converged here."), "Clean"))))) to sHead
            Move (iN - 1) to i
            While (i >= 0)
                Move Hist.aEntries[i] to E
                If (E.iErr = 0 and E.iAuto = 0 and E.iSuggest = 0) Begin
                    If (E.sProgram = CS_ModProgressDeepScanLabel) ;
                        Move (CellTipHtml("c-clean", ("Scan exhausted - this cycle found nothing a fix plan" ;
                            + " can act on (remaining findings are informational)."), CS_Check)) to sCleanTd
                    Else ;
                        Move (CellTipHtml("c-clean", ("Clean - no compiler errors and nothing actionable left" ;
                            + " (remaining warnings are informational / out of scope)."), CS_Check)) to sCleanTd
                End
                Else ;
                    Move (CellHtml("", "")) to sCleanTd
                Move (sRows + (RowHtml("", (CellHtml("l", E.sDate)) ;
                    + (CellHtml("l", (SeriesText(Self, E.sProgram)))) ;
                    + (CellHtml("c-err", (String(E.iErr)))) + (CellHtml("c-warn", (String(E.iWarn)))) ;
                    + (CellHtml("c-scan", (String(E.iScan)))) ;
                    + (CellHtml("c-auto", (String(E.iAuto)))) + (CellHtml("c-rev", (String(E.iSuggest)))) ;
                    + (CellHtml("l", E.sDfVersion)) + (CellHtml("l", E.sPlatform)) ;
                    + sCleanTd))) to sRows
                Decrement i
            Loop
            // The table in its frame. The page scrolls, and the table's header row stays in view (modprogress.css).
            Move ((DivOpen("mph-table")) ;
                + (TableHtml("", (TheadHtml(sHead)) + (TbodyHtml(sRows)))) ;
                + CS_DivEnd) to sRows
            Move (sHtml + sRows + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml
            Function_Return sHtml
        End_Function

        // The clipboard export of the same history (Nils 2026-07-19: the testers are consultants -
        // a pasteable progress table for THEIR customers). Plain text with TAB-separated columns:
        // tabs paste into Excel as columns and read fine in an e-mail. Two deliberate divergences
        // from the on-screen table: rows run OLDEST -> NEWEST (the export's audience reads it as
        // the burn-down story - start high, end low - while the dialog serves the working user
        // newest-first), and the Clean check mark becomes the words Clean / Exhausted (a check
        // glyph survives some paste targets poorly). Returns "" on an empty history (Copy is
        // shut without rows; this is the belt).
        Function HistoryClipboardText Returns String
            String sText sTab sNL sSeries sNoun sCleanTxt sWS
            tModProgressFile Hist
            tModProgressEntry E
            Integer iN i iFirstWarn iLastWarn

            Get ReadModProgress of ghoApplication to Hist
            Move (SizeOfArray(Hist.aEntries)) to iN
            If (iN = 0) ;
                Function_Return ""

            Move (Character(9)) to sTab
            Move (Character(13) + Character(10)) to sNL

            // Same series walk as HistoryHtml's trend line: latest entry vs the FIRST entry of the
            // SAME series (programs and Deep Scan laps interleave in the file).
            Move Hist.aEntries[iN - 1] to E
            Move (ModProgressTotalCount(E)) to iLastWarn
            Move E.sProgram to sSeries
            Move 0 to i
            While (Hist.aEntries[i].sProgram <> sSeries)
                Increment i
            Loop
            Move (ModProgressTotalCount(Hist.aEntries[i])) to iFirstWarn
            Move (ModProgressCountNoun(sSeries)) to sNoun

            Get psSWSFile of ghoApplication to sWS
            Move ("Modernization progress - " + sWS + sNL) to sText
            Move (sText + "Exported: " + String(CurrentDateTime()) + sNL) to sText
            Move (sText + (SeriesText(Self, sSeries)) + " " + sNoun + ": " + String(iFirstWarn) + " -> " + String(iLastWarn)) to sText
            If (iFirstWarn > iLastWarn) ;
                Move (sText + " (" + String(iFirstWarn - iLastWarn) + " fewer)") to sText
            Move (sText + sNL + sNL) to sText

            // Warnings and findings in their own columns, as in the table.
            Move (sText + "When" + sTab + "Program" + sTab + "Errors" + sTab + "Warnings" + sTab + "Findings" + sTab + "Auto-fix" + sTab + "Review" + sTab + "Target" + sTab + "Clean" + sNL) to sText
            Move 0 to i
            While (i < iN)
                Move Hist.aEntries[i] to E
                Move "" to sCleanTxt
                If (E.iErr = 0 and E.iAuto = 0 and E.iSuggest = 0) Begin
                    If (E.sProgram = CS_ModProgressDeepScanLabel) ;
                        Move "Exhausted" to sCleanTxt
                    Else ;
                        Move "Clean" to sCleanTxt
                End
                Move (sText + E.sDate + sTab + (SeriesText(Self, E.sProgram)) + sTab + String(E.iErr) + sTab + String(E.iWarn) + sTab + String(E.iScan) + sTab + String(E.iAuto) + sTab + String(E.iSuggest) + sTab + E.sDfVersion + sTab + sCleanTxt + sNL) to sText
                Increment i
            Loop
            Function_Return sText
        End_Function

        // Row 0: the history. Its heading is the page's title, beside the dashboard's progress glyph (trend).
        Object oHistoryPage is a cFTHtmlPage
            Set piRowIndex to 0
            Set piColumnSpan to 34
            Set pbFillHeight to True        // the body scrolls in the page, under its title
            Set psLabel to "Modernization progress"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftpage ftg-trend"
            /* A SAMPLE FOR THE STUDIO'S DESIGNER, which draws a literal psHtml: HistoryHtml's markup with four made-up
               laps, so the Designer shows the table where the class would show its Lorem ipsum. The program never
               shows it - the panel's Activating renders the real history before the page loads (RefreshHistory). */
            Set psHtml to """
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="CssStyle/modprogress.css">
            <div class="mph">
                <div class="mph-sub">4 entries &middot; DFRefactor.src warnings 70 &rarr; 4 <span class="mph-down">(&#9660; 66 fewer)</span></div>
                <div class="mph-spark">
                    <div class="sp-b e" style="height:100%"></div>
                    <div class="sp-b e" style="height:58%"></div>
                    <div class="sp-b" style="height:17%"></div>
                    <div class="sp-b now" style="height:5%"></div></div>
                <div class="mph-meta"><span>2026-09-22 08:58 &middot; 70</span>
                    <span><i class="lg-e"></i>errors present<i class="lg-c"></i>errors cleared<i class="lg-n"></i>latest</span>
                    <span>2026-09-30 10:12 &middot; 4</span></div>
                <div class="mph-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr><th class="l">When</th><th class="l">Program</th><th>Err</th><th>Warn</th><th>Find</th><th>Auto</th><th>Review</th>
                                <th class="l">Target</th><th class="l">Platform</th><th>Clean</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td class="l">2026-09-30 10:12</td><td class="l">DFRefactor.src</td><td class="c-err">0</td><td class="c-warn">4</td>
                                <td class="c-scan">0</td><td class="c-auto">0</td><td class="c-rev">0</td><td class="l">26.0</td><td class="l">x64</td>
                                <td class="c-clean">&#10003;</td></tr>
                            <tr><td class="l">2026-09-27 15:22</td><td class="l">DFRefactor.src</td><td class="c-err">0</td><td class="c-warn">12</td>
                                <td class="c-scan">0</td><td class="c-auto">3</td><td class="c-rev">4</td><td class="l">26.0</td><td class="l">x64</td><td></td></tr>
                            <tr><td class="l">2026-09-24 10:44</td><td class="l">DFRefactor.src</td><td class="c-err">6</td><td class="c-warn">41</td>
                                <td class="c-scan">0</td><td class="c-auto">11</td><td class="c-rev">9</td><td class="l">26.0</td><td class="l">x64</td><td></td></tr>
                            <tr><td class="l">2026-09-22 08:58</td><td class="l">DFRefactor.src</td><td class="c-err">15</td><td class="c-warn">70</td>
                                <td class="c-scan">0</td><td class="c-auto">18</td><td class="c-rev">12</td><td class="l">26.0</td><td class="l">x64</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
            """
        End_Object

        /* Row 2, THE BUTTONS: Copy, Reset and Close, framework buttons (cFTWebButton, RDCFlexTron) at the bottom
           right. Each one's work runs in its OnButtonClick, after the web click has returned (the library's
           click relay), so Reset's Yes/No box, Copy's acknowledgement and Close_Panel can run there. 11 columns
           (78 px) each fit the captions (Copy ~70 px, Reset ~72, Close ~72, measured 2026-09-30). Copy and
           Reset are shut while the history is empty (RefreshHistory). */
        Object oCopyBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piRowIndex to 2
            Set piColumnIndex to 1
            Set piColumnSpan to 11
            Set psCaption to "Copy"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-copy"
            Set psToolTip to "Copy this history as a text table to the Windows clipboard - ready to paste into an e-mail or Excel."

            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send DoCopy of (oModProgressHistory_dg(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        Object oResetBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piRowIndex to 2
            Set piColumnIndex to 12
            Set piColumnSpan to 11
            Set psCaption to "Reset"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-eraser mph-reset"   // mph-reset: its hover warns, as the chip's did (modprogress.css)
            Set psToolTip to "Clear this workspace history and start a fresh baseline. Cannot be undone."

            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send DoReset of (oModProgressHistory_dg(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        Object oCloseBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piRowIndex to 2
            Set piColumnIndex to 23
            Set piColumnSpan to 11
            Set psCaption to "Close"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-close"

            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send DoClose of (oModProgressHistory_dg(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object
    End_Object

    // cFTModalPanel fits the host to the panel, when it is shown and on every resize.
    Set phoClientHost to (oWebHost(Self))

    // Each open: the history may have changed while the dialog was closed.
    Procedure Activating
        Forward Send Activating
        Send RefreshHistory
    End_Procedure

    /* THE PAGE AND THE BUTTONS from the history file - on each open and after a Reset. UpdateHtml keeps the
       page for a mount still to come and pushes it to a page that is up; the buttons' setters WebSet the same
       way. */
    Procedure RefreshHistory
        Handle hoHost hoPage hoCopy hoReset
        String sHtml
        Boolean bAny
        tModProgressFile Hist
        Move (oWebHost(Self)) to hoHost
        Move (oHistoryPage(hoHost)) to hoPage
        Move (oCopyBtn(hoHost)) to hoCopy
        Move (oResetBtn(hoHost)) to hoReset
        Get ReadModProgress of ghoApplication to Hist
        Get HistoryHtml of hoHost Hist to sHtml
        Move (SizeOfArray(Hist.aEntries) > 0) to bAny
        Send UpdateHtml of hoPage sHtml
        Send UpdateEnabled of hoCopy bAny
        Send UpdateEnabled of hoReset bAny
    End_Procedure

    // Reset (clear this workspace's history), from the Reset button's OnButtonClick - after the web click, where
    // the Yes/No box can open. Confirmed -> delete the file (per-workspace; others keep theirs) -> re-render (now
    // the empty placeholder, with Copy and Reset shut), pushed at once.
    Procedure DoReset
        Integer iRet
        Get FTYesNoBox "Reset the modernization progress history for this workspace?\n\nThis clears the recorded burn-down so the next analyze starts a fresh baseline. Other workspaces keep their history.\n\nThis cannot be undone. Continue?" to iRet
        If (iRet <> MBR_Yes) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Send ResetModProgress of ghoApplication
        Send RefreshHistory
        Send CheckUpdateWebUI of (oWebHost(Self))
    End_Procedure

    // Copy the history table to the Windows clipboard, from the Copy button's OnButtonClick - after the web
    // click, where the acknowledgement box can open. rfSetClipboardText (RefactorFileIO.pkg) is the one
    // way onto the clipboard.
    Procedure DoCopy
        Boolean bOk
        String sData
        Get HistoryClipboardText of (oWebHost(Self)) to sData
        If (sData = "") ;
            Procedure_Return
        Get rfSetClipboardText sData to bOk
        If (bOk = False) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Send FTInfoBox "History copied to the Windows clipboard.\nPress Ctrl+V to paste it into an e-mail or a spreadsheet." "Copy History"
    End_Procedure

    // Close, from the Close button's OnButtonClick - after the web click, where the modal can end.
    Procedure DoClose
        Send Close_Panel
    End_Procedure

End_Object

// Pop the modal; its Activating renders the history. File-scope (like FillBackupFilesDialog) so it compiles into
// the command-bar client that Uses this .dg; the dashboard calls it via Send ...of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars)).
Procedure ShowProgressHistory
    Send Popup of (oModProgressHistory_dg(Self))
End_Procedure
